  "id": "anorexia",
  "term": "anorexia",
  "definition": "In psychology, anorexia usually refers to anorexia nervosa, a severe psychiatric disorder that often begins in adolescence and carries major medical risks and an increased risk of death. It affects both physical health and psychological functioning and is commonly addressed through early family-centered care.",
